occwl (OCC Wrapper Library)  -  not vendored, installed from upstream
  Path      none in this repository
  Upstream  https://github.com/AutodeskAILab/occwl
  Pinned to https://github.com/AutodeskAILab/occwl
            @8b536ea8b3cf977dbafc1cf0a89eaa28fa996bba  (version 3.0.0)

  A Pythonic wrapper around pythonocc.  AAGNet's graph extractor imports it,
  which is the only reason this project has it at all.

  It is installed, not copied: `install/environment.yml` names the commit above
  in its pip section, so `conda env create` fetches it from upstream.  It is not
  on PyPI, which is why the pin is a git URL rather than a version.  Nothing
  from it is redistributed with this repository.

  Licence status, stated as fact rather than inferred: upstream declares
  `license: BSD` in its conda recipe (`ci/conda/meta.yaml`) and ships no licence
  text - no LICENSE, LICENCE or COPYING file exists in its working tree, in its
  whole git history, in the GitHub licence API (which returns 404 for it), or in
  its published conda package.  Which BSD variant, and which copyright holder,
  upstream does not say.  Whoever installs it obtains it from upstream on
  upstream's terms.
